// by a '-') right before intersection X. Assume crossing at D is
// prohibited (denoted by a '%'). Assume "prime" roads (A',B',...) are
// OUT segments relative to X. A\\A' B//B' \\ // \\ // - - X - % // \\
// // \\ C'//C D'\\D * A CROSSABLE PedestrianCrossing should be added to
// A, B and C. * An UNCROSSABLE PedestrianCrossing should be added to D.
// Example 2: Simple intersection with one crossing. Assume intersection
// X was added to accommodate the crosswalk (through X, denoted by '-').
// Assume "prime" roads (A',B',...) are OUT segments relative to X.
// A\\A' \\ \\ -X- \\ \\ B'\\B * A CROSSABLE PedestrianCrossing must be
// added to either A or B, but not both because each real-world crossing
// should be represented exactly once. Duplicative crossings may be
// arbitrarily removed.
