// likely one day, but the client should stick to the "next_poll_time"
// to decide when to query the server again at the latest. Below there
// is an example response from the server. Let's assume the client calls
// the service at 17:59:45. The client receives the message and,
// assuming its current time is between [17:59:45, 18:00:00), it
// displays "inactive". When the current time becomes 18:00:00 it
// displays "outside working hours". At 18:00:40 the client issues
// another rpc which will return the availabilities for the next minute.
// The original response looks like availabilities { time_range {
// start_time: 17:59:45 end_time: 18:00:00 } status { inactive {} } }
// availabilities { time_range { start_time: 18:00:00 end_time: 18:00:45
