	// ranges which are ordered chronologically. The first one starts at the
	// time of the request or before, and is guaranteed to contain the
	// request time. That means the first element always indicates the
	// current status of a user. A client that wants to display a user's
	// availability in real time should display the availability whose time
	// range contains the current time.
