	// as popups, typically using CSS z-index to hover above main content
	// and occlude it.
	//   "SCROLLABLE" - Scrollable layout type includes large inline
	// interstitials that are typically inserted before the main content
	// starts, and require the user to scroll past them.
	//   "STANDALONE" - Standalone layout type includes interstitials that
	// appear as a separate page, and typically redirect the browser to main
	// content after a delay or a user action.
	//   "DENSITY" - Could be any type of layout. Usually it means it's an
